  "accessionCode": "CCX-A-13161",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A shallow lidless vessel of fired silt clay with two rope lugs, burnished inside and left rough outside, made to carry a divided pit culture up a terrace slope in one journey. It was thrown and fired on the morning of a division in the autumn of 2295 and used within the hour, which is the ordinary practice and the reason the collection can date it to the day. The interior carries a dark organic film that is the remains of what it held. It has never been cleaned and the accession record forbids cleaning it, in a line added by hand.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
